() Tj
T*
(PRECISE CALCIUM-TO-SPIKE INFERENCE USING BIOPHYSICAL GENERATIVE MODELS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This Figshare repository is in support of "Precise calcium-to-spike inference using biophysical) Tj
T*
(generative models" from Broussard et al. It contains the data exports, MATLAB plotting functions,) Tj
T*
(Python plotting scripts, shared utilities, and rendered table assets used to reproduce the) Tj
T*
(manuscript figures and supplementary figures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Figure panels are generated by scripts in the matching figure* or supp_figure* directory. MATLAB) Tj
T*
(panels are generally script-style functions named for the figure and panel range. Python panels are) Tj
T*
(installable console entry points defined in setup.py.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Environment and paths) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Use MATLAB for .m scripts and a conda or venv Python environment for .py scripts. From the) Tj
T*
(repository root on a Windows machine:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    python -m venv .venv) Tj
T*
(    .\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    pip install -e .) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Conda works equivalently after activating the target environment. Python entry points resolve data) Tj
T*
(and output paths back to this project checkout, not to the environment's site-packages directory. If) Tj
T*
(launching from an unusual working directory, set GCAMP_FIGSHARE_ROOT or FIGSHARE_PROJECT_DIR to the) Tj
T*
(repository root.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(For MATLAB, add the full checkout to the path before running figure scripts:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    repoRoot = 'C:\\path\\to\\Figshare';) Tj
T*
(    addpath\(genpath\(repoRoot\)\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(After that, run scripts from the repository root or from their figure directory. Outputs are written) Tj
T*
(to the figure directory or its output subdirectory when saving is enabled.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Main figure contents) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- figure1: jGCaMP response properties. Panels cover single-spike responses, response) Tj
T*
(  amplitude/kinetic summaries, paired-pulse and multi-spike response behavior, and jGCaMP8f in vivo) Tj
T*
(  quiescent-event examples with last-aligned averages and fast decay summaries.) Tj
T*
(- figure2: stopped-flow and bouton kinetic measurements across GCaMP variants. Scripts plot on/off) Tj
T*
(  kinetics, stopped-flow rise times, bouton rise comparisons, Hill-style summaries, 10-pulse) Tj
T*
(  responses, decay summaries, and kinetic contribution analyses.) Tj
T*
(- figure3: biophysical generative model fits and spike-inference examples. MATLAB scripts show) Tj
T*
(  stopped-flow and bouton/state fits for GCaMP6f, jGCaMP7f, and jGCaMP8f. The Python script compares) Tj
T*
(  biophysical and linear SMC inference on simulated excitatory/inhibitory examples.) Tj
T*
(- figure4: spike-inference performance on jGCaMP8f data. MATLAB scripts plot example) Tj
T*
(  continuous/discrete spike predictions and correlation versus smoothing width for excitatory and) Tj
T*
(  inhibitory cells using correlation_tbl_jG8f.mat. The Python script plots matched bias/recall-style) Tj
T*
(  distributions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Supplementary figure contents) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- supp_figure1: saturation, elongation, and related controls for jGCaMP8f multi-spike protocols.) Tj
T*
(- supp_figure2: EGTA/BAPTA clamp comparisons, including data and simulations for OGB and jGCaMP8f.) Tj
T*
(- supp_figure3: magnesium and ionic-strength effects on steady-state fluorescence and kinetics) Tj
T*
(  across sensors.) Tj
ET
